<title>AUSTRIA: Austrian train collision injures 12 people.</title>
<headline>Austrian train collision injures 12 people.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Austrian trains collided early on Wednesday, injuring 12 people, one of them seriously, a spokesman for the state railway OeBB told Reuters.</p>
<p>A regional passenger train rammed into a goods train at the station of Hilm-Kematen in Lower Austria, some 150 kilometres (90 miles) west of Vienna.</p>
<p>The spokesman said the passenger train had apparently been mistakenly redirected to the same platform as the goods train.</p>
</text>
